    "name": "Baby Bok Choi",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Bok choy isa nutrient-dense,, mild-flavored Chinese cabbage(</span><i><em class=\"lexical-text-editor--italic\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Brassica rapa subsp. chinensis</em></i><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">) known for its crisp, white, or light green celery-like stalks and smooth, dark green leaves. Unlike traditional cabbage, it does not form a head, but rather a cluster, offering a flavor profile between cabbage and water chestnuts with a subtle peppery undertone.</span></p>",
